          Appropriations Committee Fiscal Summary

                                AB 1 x (Villaraigosa)

Hearing Date:3/17/99            Amended:3/4/99 
                                
Consultant: Karen French        Policy Vote:Education  10-0
____________________________________________________________ 

BILL SUMMARY: 

AB 1X establishes the California Peer Assistance and Review  
Program (CPARP) to provide evaluation and assistance to  
veteran teachers.  The program components are as follows:
 Eliminates the existing Mentor Teacher Program (MTP) on  
  July 1, 2001.   The MTP primarily provides assistance and  
  guidance to new teachers and is funded at $5680 per  
  mentor teacher.
 Specifies that a school district accepting funds for the  
  new CPARP agrees to negotiate the development and  
  implementation of the program with the exclusive  
  representative of the certificated employees in the  
  district.
 Provides incentive funding of $2,800 per consulting  
  teacher for districts that implement the program by July  
  1, 2000 and of $1,000 for those, which implement by July  
  1, 2001. 
 Imposes a "hammer" for school districts that do not  
  participate in the program by July 1, 2001, which makes  
  districts ineligible for staff development day buyout  
  funding ($222 million), school development plan funding  
  ($20 million), and funding equal to that included in the  
  State Budget for the Beginning Teacher Support and  
  Assessment (BTSA) Program ($72 million).
 Appropriates $125 million in the 1999-2000 fiscal year to  
  fund both the CPARP and the MTP.   Appropriates $82,000  
  for administration.

                         Fiscal Impact (in thousands)
 <u> 
Major Provisions </u>      <u> 1999-2000 </u>        <u> 2000-01 </u> <u> 2001-02 </u> <u> Fund </u> 

CPARP               $41,800*     $125,000    $125,000General**
